# 0. MISSION AND AUDIT AUTHORITY

Act as a principal speech-recognition systems architect, neural-network architecture researcher, audio DSP engineer, CPU inference specialist, and forensic software auditor.

Your assignment is to conduct a rigorous, narrowly scoped forensic audit of the existing SHAHAB speech-recognition engine within the AVAPARDAZ application.

This is the application's FIRST functional development stage:

**Audio Input → Audio Processing → SHAHAB Inference → Persian Speech-to-Text Output.**

SHAHAB is intended to become a project-owned, locally operating Persian ASR engine. It must eventually serve two independent application hosts:

1. The AVAPARDAZ application.
2. A future Adobe Audition integration.

The same authoritative recognition core must serve both environments. Independent, duplicated ASR implementations are not the intended architecture.

The audit has four primary objectives:

A. Establish what SHAHAB actually is today.

B. Identify material implementation defects, architectural weaknesses, and computational inefficiencies in its existing speech-to-text execution path.

C. Determine whether its current architecture can realistically evolve into the intended compact, high-accuracy, CPU-efficient recognition engine.

D. Assess whether its recognition core can be separated from application-specific dependencies and reused by a future Adobe Audition host.

**This is an audit, NOT a development task, implementation task, optimization task, or architecture-rewriting task.**

Your authority is limited to inspecting existing evidence and producing technically justified recommendations.

Do not change the application.

